<title>USA: Camden, N.J., weighs budget gap options -- paper.</title>
<headline>Camden, N.J., weighs budget gap options -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Camden, N.J., officials are considering options including layoffs and tax increases to close a budget deficit of $796,000, the Philadelphia Inquirer reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's $100 million budget fell out of balance when Gov. Christine Whitman's administration decided to give the city $8.3 million in bailout money instead of the $9 million originally allocated.</p>
<p>Another problem arose last week when the Delaware River Port Authority's payment to the city in lieu of taxes was cut by $96,000.</p>
<p>The newspaper also said Whitman is considering setting up a state oversight board for the city. Details for such a board could be announced next month, the paper said.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
